From fae5f17c972b562f6c7db54b370593f15cd06d8e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jiming Pang <discrete_brain@163.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 15:15:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 35/43] refactor(smap): consolidate cold-period logic and
 resolve struct page once per scan

Thread struct page through the helper chain to eliminate redundant
pfn_to_online_page() lookups: resolve the page up front in callers
and pass it to actc_data_lookup_entry(), actc_data_add_fast(),
set_non_anon_bm(), and add_to_bm_page() instead of having each
callee look it up independently.

Extract the duplicated end-of-period cold-counter update from
hva_to_hpa_4k(), smap_bulk_pte_cb(), and process_memslot_pages()
into a shared smap_handle_last_scan_4k() helper, consolidating
the cold_periods_inc/enqueue/add_to_bm logic that was repeated
verbatim across all three 4K scan paths.

Also: rename g_cold_period_threshold to cold_period_thresh for
brevity, and guard SMAP_MAX_NUMNODES with #ifndef to allow
override before inclusion.
